{"title":"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Brodie and Ryan are driving directly towards each other. Brodie is driving at a constant speed of 50 km/h. Ryan is driving at a constant speed of 40 km/h. If they are 120 km apart, how long will it take before they meet?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b0165de143af15c3a906284147b80a32c1d09e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1 \\text{ h } 12 \\text{ min} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1 \\text{ h } 25 \\text{ min} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 1 \\text{ h } 15 \\text{ min} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 1 \\text{ h } 33 \\text{ min} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 1 \\text{ h } 20 \\text{ min}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"709\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/a/8eaad0d01096915f0a6e778d30af025560d7be59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40 \\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{hr}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"47\" height=\"38\" /> is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e47be30176cb43ba0d3f9ee22479ef570e494f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{40}{60} \\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{min}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"56\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1760282a1bf32381dc78ae39cd0305399784d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50 \\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{hr}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"47\" height=\"38\" /> is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/7/577eba99bb7f69d8897649a36f53b2e71c2f58d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{50}{60} \\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{min}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"56\" height=\"38\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> be the time, in minutes, that it takes for them to meet. The total distance that they traveled when they met must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e6077c3ee85d47a3752838ca9b62c1072c13b64b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120 \\text{ km}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/b/d2bb8379af330aaa5d0ee2ccc215d8e859b56628.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{40}{60} + \\frac{50}{60}) \\times m = 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"172\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/0/370ca6179e0e89640faab8e6abbc0ad8c765451f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{90}{60} \\times m = 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/0/ad022fcf82eb25a79cf88333b045512a9921f60a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{2} \\times m = 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/8/8287acfee9a87a2d0f1dcb297532916882588b7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 120 \\times \\frac{2}{3} = 80 \\text{ minutes}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"209\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/a/4ba87f6ab24838ee9c9df5e1d41e5725354a4482.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80 \\text{ minutes}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/6/99643452a17079ed2e5dbde32ac1e4356117848a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(E) } 1 \\text{ h } 20 \\text{ min}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"128\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 19 (page does not exist)\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)